Changelog: 31-10-2026 12:59:38

Added. The Operating Mode helper on the ROG Xbox Ally X (owner, 31-10-2026): the Operating Mode page's Watt limits
row installs it with one administrator prompt (helper/install-helper.ps1) and removes it again; install.ps1
--uninstall removes it with its own remover. It is the scheduled task \Windows Portable Suite\Operating Mode, which
runs helper/operating-mode.ps1 from C:\Program Files\windows-portable-suite\ as SYSTEM, when the portal starts it
(users may start it, nothing more), 5 s after every change of the power source (Kernel-Power 105), and 20 s and 2
minutes after a sign-in, so the portal's mode holds after a restart too, once Armoury Crate's services have applied
theirs (owner, 31-10-2026). It applies
the whole mode the portal names in C:\ProgramData\windows-portable-suite\operating-mode (one letter, the only file
users may write there): the power plan, Windows' power mode and the three watt limits through ASUS WMI
(AsusAtkWmi_WMNB DEVS), from its own table, which a test keeps equal to operating_mode.py's. Windows mode's slow
limit on battery is measured now (31-10-2026, Cinebench on battery: 21 W held at the slow limit's 100 % for three
minutes), so every mode has all three limits: 17 / 21 / 26 W, as on the charger. The page shows its
answer (operating-mode-result): the watts written, or why not.

