Changelog: 28-10-2026 17:00:55

Fixed. The portal's own update deleted the installed program and stopped, so the portal was gone (owner,
28-10-2026, on the Ally): the update's PowerShell window started in the portal's program folder, which Windows will
not remove while a process has it as its working directory, and install.ps1 removed the files before it found
out. The window now moves to the release folder before the installer runs ([Environment]::CurrentDirectory), and
install.ps1 puts the new program in place before the old one goes: it renames the folder, or, while a window still
holds it (an update started by an earlier portal), moves its contents; a program still running from it is refused
with nothing changed.

